RPT_INFO @ 0 [DEMO] 
##########################################################################
# BOUNDED BUFFER LIVELOCK DEMO  (model of the full-buffer deadlock)
#
#   q    = pending queue, oldest request first. A request leaves ONLY when it completes.
#   buf  = bounded FIFO of request ids, capacity 4.
#   port = ONE service per cycle (service port). A service pops buf.front().
#
# Start state: requests 4..7 already fill buf, the oldest requests
# 0..3 are still waiting in q. Demand is constant: whenever a request completes, a new
# younger one enters q.
#
# Each cycle every request in q is visited oldest-first, in order:
#   not in buf -> try to insert; if buf is full the insert fails, but the request may
#                 still burn the port to pop the front ('queue-only service');
#   in buf     -> try the port; it completes only if buf.front() is ITS OWN entry.
##########################################################################
RPT_INFO @ 0 [DEMO] 
==========================================================================
